          "text": "General appearance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, no acute distress, conversant; slightly vague historian."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal and inguinal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft and non-tender, with no masses. No palpable inguinal hernia with cough impulse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left hemiscrotum enlarged with smooth, non-erythematous skin and intact skin. Fluctuant, non-tender swelling superior and anterior to the left testis. Left testis palpated posteriorly with normal size and consistency; no discrete intratesticular solid mass. No warmth or tenderness along the epididymis or cord and no obvious cough impulse. Right testis normal size, shape and consistency, non-tender; right epididymis and cord normal. No inguinal lymph nodes."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Scrotal transillumination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Positive over the left swelling at the last visit; not repeated today."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Scrotal ultrasound"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Moderate simple left hydrocele with anechoic fluid around the left testis. Left testis normal size and echotexture, with no focal lesion and normal Doppler flow; epididymis unremarkable. Right testis and epididymis normal. No evidence of inguinal hernia or torsion. Report impression: simple left hydrocele with no sonographic evidence of testicular neoplasm."
      }
